{"case_id":"C075","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":94,"change_types":["new public entry point","new plist node type","serialization behavior change","attack-surface expansion"],"affected_functions":["plist_new_null","parse_bin_node","plist_to_bin","node_to_xml","plist_to_xml"],"reason":"The commit adds the public PLIST_NULL type and plist_new_null(), along with new binary serialization and XML rejection behavior. The existing bplist harness can reach PLIST_NULL parsing through plist_from_bin, but it only frees the parsed tree; neither harness invokes plist_new_null, plist_to_bin, or plist_to_xml. Consequently, the newly added writer behavior and the recursive XML failure path for null nodes are outside the harnesses' exercised paths.","evidence":["include/plist/plist.h adds PLIST_NULL and the public plist_new_null(void) API.","parse_bin_node now creates a PLIST_NULL node for BPLIST_NULL, which bplist_fuzzer can exercise through plist_from_bin.","plist_to_bin adds a PLIST_NULL serialization case, but bplist_fuzzer never calls plist_to_bin.","node_to_xml now returns an error for PLIST_NULL and propagates child errors recursively; plist_to_xml converts that error into NULL output and zero length.","Both existing harnesses only call their corresponding parser and plist_free, so they do not exercise constructors or serialization."],"recommended_action":"Extend the binary harness or add a round-trip/cross-format target that parses fuzz-controlled binary plists and invokes plist_to_bin and plist_to_xml, including trees containing PLIST_NULL; also directly exercise plist_new_null where appropriate and safely free any produced output."}
